ils explicitly.","maxLength":524288,"type":"string"},"comment_id":{"description":"Existing issue or pull request comment ID to update. Only valid when the workflow config sets safe-outputs.add-comment.target to '*' and the ID is present in safe-outputs.add-comment.allows-comment-ids. Use this only for comment IDs precomputed by trusted workflow steps.","type":["number","string"]},"integrity":{"description":"Trustworthiness level of the message source (e.g., \"low\", \"medium\", \"high\").","type":"string"},"item_number":{"description":"The issue, pull request, or discussion number to comment on. This is the numeric ID from the GitHub URL (e.g., 123 in github.com/owner/repo/issues/123). Can also be a temporary_id from a previously created issue in the same workflow run — use the '#aw_abc123' form; the bare 'aw_abc123' form is also accepted and normalised to '#aw_abc123'. If omitted, the tool auto-targets the issue, PR, or discussion that triggered this workflow. Auto-targeting only works for issue, pull_request, discussion, and comment event triggers — it does NOT work for schedule, workflow_dispatch, push, or workflow_run triggers. For those trigger types, always provide item_number explicitly, or the tool call will fail with an error. Required when safe-outputs.add-comment.target is '*' (any item): calls without item_number (or pr_number/pr alias) are rejected. NOTE: this field is named item_number, NOT issue_number.","type":["number","string"]},"pr":{"description":"Alias for item_number when targeting a pull request. Prefer item_number in new calls.","type":["number","string"]},"pr_number":{"description":"Alias for item_number when targeting a pull request. Prefer item_number in new calls.","type":["number","string"]},"reply_to_id":{"description":"Node ID of the discussion comment to reply to, enabling threaded discussion comments. When provided, the new comment is posted as a reply to the specified top-level discussion comment. If the given node ID belongs to a n